00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.630
David, why not tell Republicans not to vote?

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:02.630
They're voting for absolutely horrible people.

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.630
And again, it's the principle.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.630
This is not a program that activate that advocates
for not voting.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.630
And I understand if Republicans stopped voting,
then the left could easily win.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.630
But it's if you know me, you know that that's
not how I operate.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.630
I know that many will say, why aren't you
stooping to their level?

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.630
They stoop to their level and they don't care.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.630
Well, I do care.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.630
I do care.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:11.630
I'm taking the high road on that.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:12.630
But if Republicans want to insist that they
shouldn't vote because it's rigged, by all

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.630
means, go ahead and do it.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.630
And I would gladly accept Republicans losing
those two seats because they believe that

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:15.630
their voting is actually rigged.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.630
Go ahead.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.630
But in the end, I think most Republicans are
going to vote.

